\section{The workflow}{

\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=mimic_config]{mimic_config()}} sets the disclosure rules. Defaults are strict.
\item \code{\link[=profile_data]{profile_data()}} describes the real data. Protection is applied \emph{before}
anything is stored, so the description may leave the secure
environment.
\item \code{\link[=mimic]{mimic()}} builds a synthetic copy from the description. Level 1
(structure only) is the default.
\item \code{\link[=trial_run]{trial_run()}} runs the researcher's script on the copy and checks its
output with \code{\link[=inspect]{inspect()}} in advance. In the script, \code{\link[=safe_count]{safe_count()}},
\code{\link[=safe_summary]{safe_summary()}} and \code{\link[=safe_model]{safe_model()}} make output that passes, and
\code{\link[=describe_output]{describe_output()}} says what each file shows.
\item \code{\link[=real_run]{real_run()}} runs it on the real data and returns a safe error report
if it fails.
\item \code{\link[=inspect]{inspect()}} checks the output and gives a clear approve / needs
changes verdict per file; \code{\link[=write_report]{write_report()}} writes it for the approver.
\item \code{\link[=record_release]{record_release()}} keeps what was released in a register, so later
output is checked against it.
